WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.100
A din attack sold for $3,995, pricing cellular calls as a luxury.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:12.080
22 years later, the Motorola C113 went wholesale for less than $30. This is First Principles

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:18.960
Daily, episode 141. The drop, the module habit that kept the old price intact, the redesign

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:24.280
that deleted whole parts, the gap that still sits above raw materials, and the volume rule

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:29.600
that decides the next target. That collapse did not come from cheaper atoms alone. It

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:34.380
It came from redesigns that listed what a radio actually had to do, then removed every

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.080
part that did none of those jobs.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:40.460
Early cellular phones copied car radios and military transceivers.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:46.260
Designers started with modules already on the shelf, an RF power amplifier in one place,

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:51.060
a frequency synthesizer in another, a separate nickel cadmium battery pack.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:54.220
They bolted those blocks into a cast metal housing.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:58.100
Each module had already been qualified for some other product line.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:02.900
line. The only question left was whether the module would fit the new case. The finished

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:08.720
device weighed nearly 2 pounds, inside sat dozens of discrete boards, cables, and connectors.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:14.640
Every supplier quoted its piece as a finished sub-assembly. The handset price therefore stayed

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:19.500
close to the sum of those supplier prices. Nobody in the chain owned a different question.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:24.860
What would the radio cost if functions shared fewer silicon dies? What if the antenna

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:29.660
were stamped from sheet metal instead of wound by hand. The convention reproduced itself.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:35.320
Each new model simply shrank the same collection of purchased blocks. The nickel-cadmium cells

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:42.040
alone already carried a material cost above $200 in the dinotack era. Discrete circuitry, wiring

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:47.480
harnesses, and the machined enclosure added far more than those cells. Suppliers had no reason

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:52.420
to redesign their own modules. The handset maker treated those modules as fixed inputs.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:57.440
incremental improvement preserved the original partition, separate boards, separate

00:01:57.440 --> 00:01:59.160
connectors, separate invoices.

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:04.520
The decisive shift was to stop treating the handset as proven modules, and start treating

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:06.380
it as required electrical functions.

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:11.620
The radio still had to generate, amplify, and filter signals at cellular frequencies.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:16.180
It still had to turn voice into digital bits and turn those bits back into voice.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:18.640
It still needed a stable power source.

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:24.420
Listed that way, with no reference to existing hardware, the functions could be asked a new question.

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:26.800
Which of them could share the same silicon?

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:32.280
Baseband processors that had lived on separate chips were integrated with the RF transceiver.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:34.420
One move, three deletions.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.480
Multiple interconnects disappeared.

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:38.140
Board area shrank.

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:41.060
Each interface no longer had to be tested twice.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:44.220
Once on each side of a connector that no longer existed.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:46.700
The antenna changed in the same pass.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:54.660
A discreet helical element, wound and bought as its own part, became a stamped metal pattern printed directly onto the plastic housing.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:56.520
The pattern still radiated.

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:01.320
It did that job with far fewer assembly steps and with no separate procurement line.

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:05.200
Battery chemistry moved from nickel cadmium to lithium ion.

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:09.700
Higher energy density meant smaller cells while talk time stayed acceptable.

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:12.840
Each change hit a different term in the cost equation.

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:15.840
Integration cut the number of purchased components.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:21.680
resistance, stamping replace precision machining, denser cells cut volume, and a smaller volume

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:24.000
meant less plastic and less metal in the case.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:30.340
The GSM Association, the GSMA, later bundled demand through its emerging market handset

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:30.800
program.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:36.540
Ten operators, roughly six million units, that commitment let the same platform run on

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:41.040
high volume lines in Asia, where the cost of each additional handset fell further.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:47.480
The program's second phase target, wholesale below $30, was announced in late 2005 for

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:49.260
delivery in early 2006.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:53.940
That target reflected the pile of those steps, not one miracle part.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:58.020
A fair objection, integration raises mask-set costs up front.

00:03:58.580 --> 00:04:02.740
Six million units spread those fixed costs until the per-unit penalty disappeared.

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:06.860
Another fair objection, a stamped antenna gives up efficiency.

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:11.800
The design traded a few decibels of gain for the deletion of an entire purchased part,

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.540
and the labor attached to it.

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:18.260
The handset still met the talk time and standby requirements the operators had set.

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:22.440
There is a useful way to see how far such a redesign has actually gone.

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:27.280
Imagine a magic wand that arranges the raw atoms into the finished thing for free.

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:31.380
You would pay only for the silicon, the metals, and the battery materials.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:33.560
That material bill is the floor.

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:39.280
4. The idiot index is how many times the finished price exceeds that floor. A high index means

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:44.480
the design and the process, not the atoms, are what you are buying. On the dinotax, supplier

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:49.380
subassembly set the price, and the sales materials were already only a slice of what the

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:55.140
enclosure and the wiring added. Most of what a buyer paid was partition, boards, connectors,

00:04:55.480 --> 00:05:01.600
machining, and the right to stop asking. By the first quarter of 2006, the C-113 and its

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:08.520
variant. The C-113A met the wholesale target. Talktime reached as much as 450 minutes,

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:16.140
standby reached 330 hours, and earlier phase 1 target below $40 X factory had already been

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:22.000
hit in 2005 on the same platform family. The new idiot index set against the raw silicone,

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:27.840
metals, and battery materials in each unit sits far lower than the dinotax. The remaining

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:29.800
Getting distance to that floor is still wide.

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:35.020
Semiconductors, even integrated, keep substantial value added by design and fabrication.

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:40.480
Lithography, doping and packaging still add layers you cannot strip out without losing

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:41.480
the functions themselves.

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:47.700
The accepted trade-offs were a thinner feature set, no color screens, no cameras, durability

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:48.840
ahead of refinement.

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:53.660
Those choices held the design inside the cost envelope operators needed for people

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:55.040
who had never had a handset.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:06:01.192
One principle travels. Integration pays only when volume is large enough to amortize

00:06:01.192 --> 00:06:06.832
the mask sets and the test development. The GSMA's 6 million unit commitment was exactly

00:06:06.832 --> 00:06:12.372
that volume. Without it, merging baseband and RF onto shared silicon would have looked

00:06:12.372 --> 00:06:17.992
expensive, because the mask cost would have sat on two few phones. A second principle travels

00:06:17.992 --> 00:06:23.332
further. The largest cuts came from removing entire categories of parts, not from bargaining

00:06:23.332 --> 00:06:29.332
a lower price on the parts that remained. A helical antenna negotiated down 10% is still a helical

00:06:29.332 --> 00:06:35.212
antenna, still a supplier, still an assembly step. A stamped pattern on the housing is a category

00:06:35.212 --> 00:06:40.312
that no longer has a purchase order. The same sequence now fits any radio that still carries

00:06:40.312 --> 00:06:45.612
legacy module boundaries. List the required functions, merge what silicon can merge,

00:06:46.252 --> 00:06:51.252
stamp or print what metal can replace, then ask whether anyone has committed enough units for

00:06:51.252 --> 00:06:56.432
the fixed cost to vanish per phone, which other high-volume electronic products still prices

00:06:56.432 --> 00:06:59.132
itself as an assembly of yesterday's proven blocks.

00:06:59.652 --> 00:07:01.632
That's First Principles Daily for today.

00:07:02.152 --> 00:07:05.992
If this changed how you see what things cost, share it with someone who depreciated,

00:07:06.412 --> 00:07:07.952
and subscribe wherever you listen.

